window.docContents[96].resolve({"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Mm.Mremap/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Mm___Mremap":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Mm › Mremap.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the computational proof and symbolic proof 6 headline theorems depend on it 131 of 166 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nLinux Virtual Memory mremap SyscallTrusted model of the Linux AArch64 mremap syscall (mm/mremap.c, include/uapi/linux/mman.h), defining Memory.remapRw, SYS_MREMAP, MREMAP_MAYMOVE, and execMremap.\n\n\n\ndef remapRwL29–54 ↗#Move or resize a non-frozen Perm.rw range [oldBase, oldBase + oldSize) onto [newBase, newBase + newSize):* frozen bytes ((m.perm a).frozen) are unconditionally preserved;* for any non-frozen byte a in [newBase, newBase + newSize) at offset off := (a - newBase).toNat, maps some (some p, b) where for off < oldSize (src := oldBase + off) b = m.read8 src and p = { Perm.rw with lazyFree := m.isLazyFree src, anon := m.isAnon src }, and for off ≥ oldSize b = 0#8 and p = Perm.rw;* for any remaining non-frozen byte a in [oldBase, oldBase + oldSize), unmaps (none);* all other bytes keep m.cells a.\n\n\n\ndef SYS_MREMAPL58–60 ↗#Linux AArch64 mremap syscall number (__NR_mremap = 216, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:597, mm/mremap.c:1964).\n\ndef MREMAP_MAYMOVEL62–63 ↗#mremap flags bit MREMAP_MAYMOVE (1, include/uapi/linux/mman.h:8).\n\ndef execMremapL65–164 ↗#mremap(old_address, old_size, new_size, flags) (__NR_mremap = 216, SYSCALL_DEFINE5(mremap), do_mremap, and mremap_at in mm/mremap.c:1559,1641,1679,2022), modeled for flags == 0 (in-place resize) and flags == MREMAP_MAYMOVE (1) on a single mapped Perm.rw anonymous range:* [INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]: any flags ≠ 0 and flags ≠ MREMAP_MAYMOVE fails closed with .Exception \"unmodeled mremap flags\";* with oldAddr := untaggedAddr X0, oldAligned := pageAlignUp oldLen, and newAligned := pageAlignUp newLen:* strips any AArch64 user TBI tag from oldAddr := untaggedAddr X0 (mm/mremap.c:2096);* rejects unaligned oldAddr, newLen == 0, or newLen > USER_VA_LIMIT (PAGE_ALIGN(new_len) == 0 || PAGE_ALIGN(new_len) > TASK_SIZE in check_mremap_params, mm/mremap.c:2028-2045) with -EINVAL;* fails closed with .Exception \"unmodeled mremap (old_size == 0)\" when oldLen == 0 or oldLen > 2 ^ 64 - PAGE_SIZE (where C PAGE_ALIGN(old_len) wraps to 0);* [INTENTIONAL_OVERAPPROX]: queries s.oracle.mremapRefusal s.oracleIdx == some .enomem immediately after check_mremap_params, consuming s.nextOracle and returning -ENOMEM (check_map_count_against_split_early before vma_lookup, mm/mremap.c:2039-2042, plus later may_expand_vm refusals at mm/mremap.c:1870);* when oldAddr.toNat + oldAligned > USER_VA_LIMIT: returns -EFAULT if the starting page at oldAddr is above USER_VA_LIMIT or unmapped (vma_lookup miss), returns oldAddr on newAligned == oldAligned (MREMAP_NO_RESIZE, mm/mremap.c:1688), returns -EINVAL on newAligned < oldAligned (MREMAP_SHRINK -> shrink_vma -> do_vmi_munmap, mm/mremap.c:897-906,1805, mm/vma.c:1717, regardless of MREMAP_MAYMOVE), and returns -EFAULT on newAligned > oldAligned (old_len > vma->vm_end - addr, mm/mremap.c:1849);* if [oldAddr, oldAddr + oldAligned) intersects any frozen byte, fails closed with .Exception \"mremap on frozen memory\";* if [oldAddr, oldAddr + oldAligned) is completely unmapped (s.mem.canMap oldAddr oldAligned), returns -EFAULT (vma_lookup miss in check_prep_vma, mm/mremap.c:1787,2047);* if [oldAddr, oldAddr + oldAligned) is not uniformly some Perm.rw or not anonymous, fails closed with .Exception;* [INTENTIONAL_OVERAPPROX]: if s.oracle.mremapRefusal s.oracleIdx == some .efault, consumes s.nextOracle, leaves s.mem unchanged, and returns -EFAULT (old_len > vma->vm_end - addr in check_prep_vma, mm/mremap.c:1849, over-approximating adjacent anonymous mappings that remain unmerged vm_area_structs in the kernel maple tree);* otherwise (mremapRefusal == none): proceeds with in-place resize (flags == 0) or MREMAP_MAYMOVE relocation via sanitizeMmapAddr mUnmapped cand newAligned.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Mm/Mremap.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Mm.Mremap/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Mm___Mremap"}});